<controls:ChildWindow x:Class="MMONavigator.Views.WatcherConfigurationDialog"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:local="clr-namespace:MMONavigator"
             xmlns:helpers="clr-namespace:MMONavigator.Helpers"
             xmlns:controls="clr-namespace:MMONavigator.Controls"
             Title="Configure Watcher" Height="700" Width="600"
             WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" ResizeMode="NoResize"
             Background="#2D2D30" Foreground="White">
    <Window.Resources>
        <BooleanToVisibilityConverter x:Key="BooleanToVisibilityConverter" />
        <local:InverseBooleanToVisibilityConverter x:Key="InverseBooleanToVisibilityConverter" />
    </Window.Resources>
    <Grid Margin="15">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
            <RowDefinition Height="40" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
            <Grid Margin="5">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Orientation="Vertical" Margin="0,0,0,5">
                    <TextBlock
                        TextWrapping="Wrap"
                        Margin="0,0,0,5" FontWeight="Bold">
                        Setup your current game profile or create a new one.
                    </TextBlock>
                    <TextBlock
                        x:Name="ExtraContent"
                        TextWrapping="Wrap"
                        Margin="0,0,0,5" FontWeight="Bold"
                        Visibility="Collapsed">
                        Pantheon - Rise of the Fallen, write to the system clipboard. 
                        The coordinate system is a "Standard Map" coordinate system, or Right Handed, where as you head East the 
                        x coordinate gets more positive. Log entries are made in "x z y f" format, where f is the direction you are facing.
                        <LineBreak />
                        <LineBreak />
                        Others, like EverQuest or Project 1999,
                        log to a file by character name. In this case, you may need to turn on logging in your game and each
                        character will need its own game profile. The coordinate system is an "Inverted Map", or LeftHanded, 
                        where as you head West the x coordinate gets more positive. Log entries are made in "y x z" format.
                        <LineBreak />
                        <LineBreak />
                        In both Pantheon and EverQuest, the program updates when the user executes the /loc command in the game. 
                        You can create a macro to execute this command with a wait between other executions. /loc /wait 1 as many times as the macro tool allows.
                        <LineBreak />
                        <LineBreak />
                        This program does not packet sniff. Many games can be made to write coordinates to a log file. Consult your game to determine how. 
                        This program is regularly used with Pantheon and has been used with Project 1999.
                        <LineBreak />
                        <LineBreak />
                        Named Shared Memory allows game developers to call directly into this application instead of this application reading game log files or clipboard. You would have special instructions from your game to use this setting.
                    </TextBlock>

                    <Button Style="{StaticResource MainButtonStyle}"
                            Content="Read More"
                            x:Name="ReadMoreBtn"
                            Click="ReadMore_Click"
                            Width="100"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                            Margin="0 5 0 5" />
                </StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Text="Game Profile:" Margin="0,0,0,5" FontWeight="Bold" />

                <Grid Grid.Row="2" Margin="0,0,0,15">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ComboBox x:Name="ProfileComboBox" 
                              IsEditable="True" 
                              Height="22"
                              FontSize="8pt"
                              Style="{StaticResource MainEditableComboBoxStyle}"
                              helpers:ClickThroughBehavior.IsEnabled="True"
                              SelectionChanged="ProfileComboBox_SelectionChanged" />
                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="1"  Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,0">
                    <Button x:Name="AddProfileButton" 
                            Content="+" 
                            Width="20" 
                            Margin="5,0,0,0"
                            Click="AddProfile_Click"
                            ToolTip="Add Profile" Style="{StaticResource PrimaryButtonStyle}"
                            FontWeight="Bold" />
                    <Button x:Name="DuplicateProfileButton" Content="&#xE8C8;"
                            FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets" Width="20" Margin="5,0,0,0"
                            Click="DuplicateProfile_Click"
                            ToolTip="Duplicate Profile" Style="{StaticResource PrimaryButtonStyle}"
                            FontWeight="Bold" Visibility="Collapsed" />
                    <Button x:Name="RemoveProfileButton" Content="-" Width="20"
                            Margin="5,0,0,0" Click="RemoveProfile_Click"
                            ToolTip="Remove Profile" Style="{StaticResource DeleteButtonStyle}"
                            FontWeight="Bold" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Grid>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Text="Watch Mode:" Margin="0,0,0,5" FontWeight="Bold" />

                <StackPanel Grid.Row="4" Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,15">
                    <RadioButton x:Name="ClipboardRadio" Content="System Clipboard" Foreground="White"
                                 Margin="0,0,20,0" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    <RadioButton x:Name="FileRadio" Content="Log File" Foreground="White"
                                 Margin="0,0,20,0" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    <RadioButton x:Name="SharedMemoryRadio" Content="Named Shared Memory" Foreground="White"
                                 VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </StackPanel>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="5" Text="Log File Path:" Margin="0,0,0,5" FontWeight="Bold"
                           Visibility="{Binding IsChecked, ElementName=FileRadio, Converter={StaticResource BooleanToVisibilityConverter}}" />

                <Grid Grid.Row="6" Margin="0,0,0,15"
                      Visibility="{Binding IsChecked, ElementName=FileRadio, Converter={StaticResource BooleanToVisibilityConverter}}">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBox x:Name="FilePathTextBox" Background="#3E3E42" Foreground="White"
                             BorderBrush="#555555" Padding="2" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    <Button Grid.Column="1" Content="..." Width="30" Margin="5,0,0,0"
                            Click="BrowseButton_Click" Background="#3E3E42" Foreground="White" />
                </Grid>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="7" Text="Log File Regex:" Margin="0,0,0,5" FontWeight="Bold"
                           Visibility="{Binding IsChecked, ElementName=FileRadio, Converter={StaticResource BooleanToVisibilityConverter}}" />

                <TextBox x:Name="RegexTextBox" Grid.Row="8" Margin="0,0,0,15"
                         Background="#3E3E42" Foreground="White" BorderBrush="#555555" Padding="2"
                         AcceptsReturn="True" TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                         Visibility="{Binding IsChecked, ElementName=FileRadio, Converter={StaticResource BooleanToVisibilityConverter}}" />

                <StackPanel Grid.Row="9" Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,15">
                    <TextBlock Text="System:" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,10,0" FontWeight="Bold" />
                    <ComboBox x:Name="SystemComboBox" 
                              Width="180" 
                              Margin="0,0,20,0" 
                              Style="{StaticResource MainComboBoxStyle}"
                              VerticalAlignment="Center"
                              SelectedValuePath="Value"
                              SelectedValue="{Binding CurrentCoordinateSystem, Mode=TwoWay}">
                        <ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate>
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Label}" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                    </ComboBox>
                    
                    <TextBlock Text="Order:" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,10,0" 
                               FontWeight="Bold" />
                    <ComboBox x:Name="OrderComboBox" Width="90" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                              helpers:ClickThroughBehavior.IsEnabled="True"
                              Style="{StaticResource MainComboBoxStyle}"
                              />
                </StackPanel>

                <CheckBox x:Name="KeyboardClickThroughCheckBox" Grid.Row="10" 
                          Visibility="Hidden"
                          Content="Keyboard Click-Through (Pass keys to game)" 
                          Foreground="White" Margin="0,0,0,15" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                          ToolTip="When enabled, the program will not consume keystrokes unless an input field is focused." />
                
                
            <StackPanel Grid.Row="11"  VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        Margin="20">
                
                <!-- Hint Subtitle -->
                <Border Background="#252526"
                        BorderBrush="#3E3E42"
                        BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="8"
                        Padding="20"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">

                    <StackPanel>
                        <!-- Large Header -->
                        <TextBlock Text="CAPTURING LOCATIONS"
                                   FontSize="14"
                                   FontWeight="Bold"
                                   Foreground="LightGray"
                                   HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                   Margin="0,0,0,12" />

                        <!-- Subtitle -->
                        <TextBlock Text="The program needs to know where your game writes the player location. It can read from the 
                        clipboard or a log file. Any game that writes coordinates to a log file can be used with this program."
                                   FontSize="12"
                                   Foreground="#CCCCCC"
                                   TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   TextAlignment="Center"
                                   LineHeight="16"
                                   Margin="0,0,0,16" />

                        <Separator Background="#3E3E42" Margin="0,0,0,16" />

                        <!-- Steps -->
                        <Grid Margin="0,0,0,16">
                            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                            <!-- Step 1 -->
                            <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Text="1." Foreground="Gold" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       Margin="0,0,8,8" />
                            <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1"
                                       Text="Pantheon: Rise of the Fallen writes to the system clipboard using standard coordinate system. This is the default. It logs when you enter /loc."
                                       Foreground="#AAAAAA" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,8" />

                            <!-- Step 2 -->
                            <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Text="2." Foreground="Gold" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       Margin="0,0,8,8" />
                            <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1"
                                       Text="EverQuest and Project 1999 writes to character specific log files. You have to enable it, which is why you need to tell this program where the log file is.
                                        It logs when you enter /loc."
                                       Foreground="#AAAAAA" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,8" />
                            
                            <!-- Step 3 -->
                            <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Text="3." Foreground="Gold" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       Margin="0,0,8,0" />
                            <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1"
                                       Text="Create a macro in your game to execute /loc. Use /wait 1 to give some time between each command. Add as many as the macro allows."
                                       Foreground="#AAAAAA" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                            
                            <!-- Step 3 -->
                            <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="0" Text="4." Foreground="Gold" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       Margin="0,0,8,0" />
                            <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1"
                                       Text="If your game writes the location continuously, this program will capture the changes."
                                       Foreground="#AAAAAA" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                        </Grid>

                        <!-- Tip / Shortcut Box -->
                        <Border Background="#1E1E1E"
                                BorderBrush="#333333"
                                BorderThickness="1"
                                CornerRadius="4"
                                Padding="10,8">
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                                <TextBlock Text="🗺️ " FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center" Foreground="Gold" />
                                <TextBlock Text="Tip: You can type in a destination location or capture your current lcoation and press the button to the right of it to copy it as a destination. Save and name existing destinations to load again in the future...."
                                           FontSize="11"
                                           Foreground="#888888"
                                           FontStyle="Italic"
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                           VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Border>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

            </StackPanel>
            </Grid>
        </ScrollViewer>

        <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Margin="0,15,0,0">
            <Button Content="OK" Width="75" Margin="0,0,10,0" Click="OkButton_Click" IsDefault="True"
                    Style="{StaticResource MainButtonStyle}" />
            <Button Content="Cancel" Width="75" Click="CancelButton_Click" IsCancel="True"
                    Style="{StaticResource MainButtonStyle}" />
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</controls:ChildWindow>